 IMPLEMENTATION NOTES (parity fidelity — web InboxPage.tsx → SwiftUI)
================================================================================
 · Data sources bound through @Observable InboxPageModel (P1/S8) with the web
   hook names kept at the Swift call sites: InboxPageData.useVehicles()
   (GET /vehicles) and InboxPageData.useAlertRules() (GET /alerts/rules). The
   loaded fleet + rules are handed to the hosted InboxBody exactly as the web
   page passes `vehicles` / `rules` props to <InboxBody/>.
 · Panels/charts/maps: the web page declares NONE of its own — it hosts the
   shared <InboxBody/> (already a built P3/P4 surface). Reproduced natively by
   hosting InboxBody(model:) with archived = false. No anonymous <GlassPanel>
   regions exist in the web source beyond InboxBody itself.
 · Data states: InboxBody renders its own loading/empty/content; the page adds a
   loading→loaded→failed phase for its two sources and surfaces TSErrorDisplay +
   Retry on a hard fetch failure (web defaults the hook data to [], so empty
   collections are still a successful load — the only manifest-declared state).
 · HIG-native: ScrollView + ViewThatFits adaptive header (macOS/iPad single row,
   iPhone stacked), TSPageTitle, design tokens only (Color.TS / Font.TS /
   TSSpacing — ADR-005), native ShareLink for the web "Copy link" (system-
   localized, zero hardcoded text), Label/SF Symbol "archivebox" for View
   archived, .refreshable pull-to-refresh.
 · i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings via
   LocalizedStringKey; zero hardcoded strings; web key names preserved.
 · a11y (ADR-015): TSPageTitle isHeader trait, .accessibilityElement(children:
   .contain) on the surface + actions, Label-provided VoiceOver labels, Dynamic
   Type via Font.TS, light/dark via tsDynamicColor tokens, ≥44pt TSButton/
   ShareLink targets.
 · Units (ADR): page renders no SI quantities; nothing stored/computed non-SI.
 · Navigation: NotificationsRouteRegistration registers .notifications →
   InboxPage; chained onto SettingsRouteRegistration in TeslaSyncApp; the shell's
   AppRouteHostRegistry renders it. "View archived" deep-links
   "/notifications/archived" via AppRouteParser.

